<attribute name="problem" nodeId="1205cd51">The EY Accelerate (EYA) for Oracle Services method details the end-to-end hybrid agile implementation approach that can be
leveraged on both on-premise and cloud Oracle services implementations at client organizations.</attribute>
<attribute name="background" nodeId="5f278597"></attribute>
<attribute name="goals" nodeId="b5bd660">&lt;p&gt;
    Key features of this method include:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    1. An &lt;strong&gt;end-to-end work breakdown structure (WBS)&lt;/strong&gt; that can be used to onboard engagement teams and
    accelerate and standardize delivery. It consists of activities, tasks, roles, input and output work products and
    deliverables that span the following key phases of a typical Oracle services implementation engagement:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;MARGIN-LEFT: 2em&quot;&gt;
    &lt;ul&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;
            Plan
        &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;
            Confirm and Design
        &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;
            Progressive Build
        &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;
            Test
        &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;
            Deploy
        &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;
            Support
        &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;
    2. A &lt;strong&gt;customizable project plan&lt;/strong&gt; that can be used as a starting point for project planning and can be
    tweaked to meet a client&apos;s specific needs. It consists of the complete work breakdown structure that can be downloaded
    in Microsoft Excel or Microsoft Project.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;
    3.&lt;strong&gt;Templates and examples&lt;/strong&gt; that can be leveraged on engagements to accelerate and standardize delivery
    as well as improve the quality of client deliverables.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;
    4.&lt;strong&gt;Information on relevant tools&lt;/strong&gt; that can be used to accelerate engagement delivery.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="application" nodeId="a16b683e"></attribute>
<attribute name="levelsOfAdoption" nodeId="1fb6ed41"></attribute>
